## Code Review Standards

### Review Checklist
```markdown
## Code Review Checklist

### Functionality
- [ ] Code implements the intended feature/fix
- [ ] Edge cases are handled appropriately
- [ ] Error handling is comprehensive
- [ ] Performance implications are considered

### Code Quality
- [ ] Code follows project style guidelines
- [ ] Functions are appropriately sized (<50 lines)
- [ ] Cyclomatic complexity is reasonable (<10)
- [ ] Variable and function names are descriptive
- [ ] Comments explain complex logic

### Testing
- [ ] Unit tests are included
- [ ] Integration tests are included (if applicable)
- [ ] Test coverage meets thresholds
- [ ] Tests are meaningful and not just for coverage

### Documentation
- [ ] Public APIs are documented
- [ ] README is updated (if applicable)
- [ ] Configuration examples are provided
- [ ] Breaking changes are documented

### Security
- [ ] No hardcoded credentials
- [ ] Input validation is implemented
- [ ] Sensitive data is handled appropriately
- [ ] Security implications are considered

### Interface Compliance
- [ ] All interface methods are implemented
- [ ] Interface contracts are satisfied
- [ ] Error types are used appropriately
- [ ] Context patterns are followed
```

### Automated Review Gates
```yaml
# .github/workflows/pr-check.yml
name: PR Checks

on:
  pull_request:
    branches: [ main ]

jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      
      - name: Set up Go
        uses: actions/setup-go@v4
        with:
          go-version: '1.24'
      
      - name: Run tests
        run: go test -v -coverprofile=coverage.out ./...
      
      - name: Check coverage
        run: |
          go tool cover -func=coverage.out | grep total | awk '{if ($3 < 75) exit 1}'
      
      - name: Run linter
        run: golangci-lint run
      
      - name: Check formatting
        run: |
          if [ "$(gofmt -l . | wc -l)" -gt 0 ]; then
            echo "Code is not formatted. Run 'gofmt -w .'"
            exit 1
          fi
```

## Development Workflow

### Feature Development Process
```go
// Feature development workflow
type FeatureWorkflow struct {
    BranchName    string
    IssueNumber   int
    Description   string
    TestsRequired bool
    DocsRequired  bool
}

func (w *FeatureWorkflow) Validate() error {
    if w.BranchName == "" {
        return fmt.Errorf("branch name is required")
    }
    
    if !strings.HasPrefix(w.BranchName, "feature/") && 
       !strings.HasPrefix(w.BranchName, "fix/") &&
       !strings.HasPrefix(w.BranchName, "docs/") {
        return fmt.Errorf("branch name must start with feature/, fix/, or docs/")
    }
    
    if w.IssueNumber <= 0 {
        return fmt.Errorf("issue number is required")
    }
    
    return nil
}

func (w *FeatureWorkflow) CreateBranch() error {
    // Create feature branch
    cmd := exec.Command("git", "checkout", "-b", w.BranchName)
    return cmd.Run()
}
```

### Code Review Process
```go
// Code review automation
type CodeReview struct {
    PRNumber      int
    Author        string
    Reviewers     []string
    Status        ReviewStatus
    Comments      []ReviewComment
}

type ReviewStatus string

const (
    ReviewStatusPending   ReviewStatus = "pending"
    ReviewStatusApproved  ReviewStatus = "approved"
    ReviewStatusChanges   ReviewStatus = "changes_requested"
    ReviewStatusDismissed ReviewStatus = "dismissed"
)

type ReviewComment struct {
    File     string
    Line     int
    Message  string
    Severity CommentSeverity
}

type CommentSeverity string

const (
    SeverityInfo    CommentSeverity = "info"
    SeverityWarning CommentSeverity = "warning"
    SeverityError   CommentSeverity = "error"
)

func (r *CodeReview) AddComment(file, message string, line int, severity CommentSeverity) {
    r.Comments = append(r.Comments, ReviewComment{
        File:     file,
        Line:     line,
        Message:  message,
        Severity: severity,
    })
}
```

